title: The Law Is Good – The Law and the Covenants
description: The law and the covenants: the law our schoolmaster to bring us to Christ, God's civil law still stands, mercy and not sacrifice, the ordinances a shadow of Christ, and the better covenant, from the teachings on the law.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-law.html
highlight: law; covenant

# One deck for the doctrine "The law & the covenants" (117 teachings), its themes given equal weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== Introduction
--- The Law Is Good [title]
overline: Doctrine · The law & the covenants
heading: The Law Is Good
sub: What the law is for, and the covenants of God.
refs: Galatians 3:24; Romans 7:12; 1 Timothy 1:8-10; Psalms 19:7; Hebrews 8:6-8
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 8966
--- The law of the LORD is perfect
big: Psalms 19:7 | mark: The law of the LORD is perfect, converting the soul
p: The law wasn't done away with, but the old covenant. Not because God's law was unjust but because we are. In His mercy He provided us a new covenant. A better testament.
p: Those who walk after the Spirit delight in His law. But those living after the flesh hate His judgments, because the law convicts them afresh, daily. So they say “that's Old Testament law. It doesn't count any more.” Despise not the law of God, but meditate on it day and night.
read: app:doctrine-law~8966 | The law of God is perfect: its purpose, grace and judgment

=== The law our schoolmaster
# from 16155, 12922, 4474
--- To bring us unto Christ
kicker: The law our schoolmaster
big: Galatians 3:24 | mark: the law was our schoolmaster to bring us unto Christ
p: How can there be revival without the law, when the law is the schoolmaster that brings the lost to repentance? How can someone know they are wrong if they don't know what's right?
p: *It shall be our righteousness, if we observe to do all these commandments* ([[Deuteronomy 6:25]]). Knowing it is impossible in our flesh to observe all, we see God's mercy revealed. The lawyer's answer was true; the Good Samaritan revealed that none of us hold to it ([[Luke 10:25-37]]).

# from 5769, 15634
--- If a man use it lawfully
kicker: The law our schoolmaster
big: 1 Timothy 1:8-9 | mark: the law is good, if a man use it lawfully; the law is not made for a righteous man, but for the lawless and disobedient
p: Paul's admonition is against the legalistic works-based false teachers, not the law itself. Many see no role for God's law today. But as we see from this list of sins, there is a clear need to maintain God's law regardless of what current year is.
p: Follow the commandments of God that it be well with you. Hold others to standards that it should lead them to understand they are sinners. Advocate for the law because it is good, when used lawfully, to punish evildoers ([[Romans 7:12]]). This shouldn't be controversial.

# from 11394, 6363
--- Love thy neighbour came from Leviticus
kicker: The law our schoolmaster
big: Leviticus 19:18 | mark: thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am the LORD
p: Many modernists believe that Jesus invented this commandment, and that it is in variance with the “more wrathful God” of the Old Testament. But they err not knowing scripture.
p: Jesus simply quoted the first commandment and Leviticus ([[Mark 12:29-31]]). And Leviticus 19:18 is in the same teachings that deal with stoning sodomites and adulterers. Both great commandments come from the same God in the same place in scripture.

# from 11427, 13242, 4048
--- The law failed because men failed
kicker: The law our schoolmaster
big: 2 Corinthians 3:6 | mark: the letter killeth, but the spirit giveth life
p: The failing of the law to achieve righteousness wasn't God's fault, but man's. The people didn't follow His statutes, and God's wrath abides on a nation that fails to sanctify themselves through them.
p: *I have set before you life and death... therefore choose life* ([[Deuteronomy 30:19]]). Because of the fault of the people, the law became a ministration of death. But in the Spirit is liberty ([[2 Corinthians 3:17]]).

# from 9563, 10328, 10307
--- The most complete ritual religion
kicker: The law our schoolmaster
big: Hebrews 10:11-12 | mark: which can never take away sins
p: God gave Israel the most well thought out and complete ritualistic religion the world has ever seen, kept holy, reflecting patterns in Heaven, and symbols of the Christ to come. And it too was a schoolmaster, to show the failings of earthly systems of sacrifices and high offices.
p: Carnal people see it as instructions for massive chapels and priests in robes and fancy vestments. But these things were not a pattern for us. *Ye are they which justify yourselves before men; but God knoweth your hearts* ([[Luke 16:15]]).
read: app:doctrine-law~16155 | The law as schoolmaster
read: app:doctrine-law~5769 | The law is good if a man use it lawfully
read: app:doctrine-law~11394 | Love thy neighbour came from Leviticus

=== God's civil law still stands
# from 13094, 12914, 10220
--- No dispensation, no repeal
kicker: God's civil law still stands
big: Hebrews 13:8 | mark: Jesus Christ the same yesterday, and to day, and for ever
p: Not the carnal ordinances and meats and diverse washings, which were a picture of Christ, but the nitty-gritty administration of a godly nation. These stand today. There is no dispensation, there is no repeal.
p: Some claim the civil laws and commandments are no longer in force, and apply it to sodomy and adultery. Yet they would not claim that murder, stealing or perjury are now ok. They simply want to call evil good. His moral law is eternal, the rules that will be enforced with a rod of iron in the Millennium.

# from 13554, 16223, 13048, 13009
--- That it may be well with thee
kicker: God's civil law still stands
big: Deuteronomy 10:12-13 | mark: which I command thee this day for thy good
p: The commandments of God aren't held over the people as punishment or “just because I say so,” but that it be well with us. Those that make obedience to the law their gospel miss the point. Its real purpose is for a righteous people to know the will of God for their lives.
p: Christianity is a religion of low-time preference. People who make the commandments the means by which they are saved become impulsive and selfish, judgmental instead of rightly judging.

# from 17426, 17151, 17956
--- The ten commandments are not impossible
kicker: God's civil law still stands
table: The commandment |
tr: No other gods; no graven image; not His name in vain | It is easy to not place another god in your life or to avoid idols.
tr: Remember the sabbath | We rest in Christ, Who is our Sabbath.
tr: Honour thy father and mother | Honoring your parents, even as adults, isn't difficult.
tr: Not kill, not commit adultery, not steal, not bear false witness, not covet | Generally easy to keep, if not perfectly. Jesus upped the ante by making it the spirit of these things.
p: If you're against the death penalty for murderers while Jesus was for it for those that curse their parents, you ain't right ([[Matthew 15:4]]).

# from 17374, 13159, 13070, 11512, 11514
--- Usury, the release and the jubilee
kicker: God's civil law still stands
big: Leviticus 25:10 | mark: proclaim liberty throughout all the land
p: In the King James Bible, usury is any interest charged on a loan, not just excessive interest ([[Deuteronomy 23:19]]). *Unto a stranger thou mayest lend upon usury* has been used as a loophole to justify the antichrists being allowed usury among Gentiles and Christians for centuries ([[Deuteronomy 23:20]]). God's law instituted a release every seven years, and a jubilee every fifty, to restore families to their land and prevent generational poverty ([[Deuteronomy 15:1-2]]).
p: The release of debts and the redemption of the servant are pictures of the salvation found in Christ. God hates the accumulation of property to the exclusion of others ([[Isaiah 5:8]]). Basically, capitalism. But that is not to say He endorsed communism, either. Fair and righteous trade.

# from 15068, 13183, 13144
--- Just weights and true witnesses
kicker: God's civil law still stands
big: Deuteronomy 19:15 | mark: at the mouth of two witnesses, or at the mouth of three witnesses, shall the matter be established
p: The purpose of requiring multiple witnesses isn't because 2 or 3 witnesses make an accusation true, but make it worthy to be judged. Quantity isn't truth. People who say “there are enough witnesses, case closed!” have judged the matter before considering anything else.
p: Divers weights are an abomination ([[Deuteronomy 25:13-16]]). God hates liars, cheats, bribery and extortion. And His laws protected marriage and virginity, protecting women and men ([[Deuteronomy 22:13-21]]). The law of God is perfect.
read: app:doctrine-law~13094 | No dispensation, no repeal
read: app:doctrine-law~17426 | The ten commandments one by one
read: app:doctrine-law~11514 | Woe to them that join house to house

=== Mercy, not sacrifice
# from 15293, 15314, 10332, 17991
--- I desired mercy
kicker: Mercy, not sacrifice
big: Hosea 6:6 | mark: I desired mercy, and not sacrifice
p: The sacrifices were always for man, not God. These things were put in place not because He desired them, but because man does. Man needs to see it, touch it, smell it. Every beast is His, the cattle upon a thousand hills ([[Psalms 50:10]]).
p: God's will for us is that we show the same mercy towards others He extended to us. Even the greatest and only true sacrifice for sin, the blood of Christ Jesus, is for our benefit, not God's.

# from 15376, 16531, 15619
--- Do justly and walk humbly
kicker: Mercy, not sacrifice
big: Micah 6:8 | mark: to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God
p: *Did ye at all fast unto me, even to me?* ([[Zechariah 7:5]]) Their fasts were self-centered, remembering their own woes. Not grand acts of fasting and weeping. To do unto others. To care for the fatherless and widows.

# from 15619 (kept in full at the author's word)
--- Woe unto you that desire the day of the LORD
kicker: Mercy, not sacrifice
big: Amos 5:25-26 | mark: the star of your god, which ye made to yourselves
p: The fake believers in their solemn assemblies, offering sacrifices as if that's what justifies them before God, and calling upon Him to come quickly... they are the very reason God's wrath is upon them ([[Amos 5:18-21]]). Israel offered sacrifices in the wilderness 40 years, and yet did not enter the promised land.
p: How much worse these who have borne the tabernacle of Moloch and Chiun, and the star of their false god, which they invented themselves. Today they call it the star of David ([[Acts 7:43]]). Today we have Catholic-made churches with idols and sacrifices of bread and wine. We have evangelicals yoked to unbelieving Jews, trying to hasten the day of the Lord, and carrying the star of their god.
read: app:doctrine-law~15619 | Woe unto you that desire the day of the Lord

# from 11499, 11501, 11502
--- Eye for eye, and the other cheek
kicker: Mercy, not sacrifice
big: Exodus 21:24 | mark: Eye for eye, tooth for tooth
p: In 1901 Hammurabi's Code was found with an eye for an eye, and the concept came to be credited to a man, taught as a savage injustice. But it is God's perfect law. Jesus calling us to turn the other cheek ([[Matthew 5:38-39]]) isn't saying the law is unjust. He's talking about our hearts storing up wrath.
p: Before a magistrate, the eye for an eye would still be justice. But we who are righteous should forgive those who wronged us. These aren't contradictory but complementary. By not walking this line, we have a society wherein there is no justice and there is no mercy. God's law is perfect, we are not.
read: app:doctrine-law~15293 | I desired mercy, and not sacrifice
read: app:doctrine-law~11499 | Eye for eye is God's law, not Hammurabi's

=== Ordinances a shadow of Christ
# from 9190, 11182, 13063
--- A shadow of things to come
kicker: Ordinances a shadow
big: Colossians 2:16-17 | mark: Which are a shadow of things to come; but the body is of Christ
p: These ordinances were given as a picture, to remind the people of the promise of the coming Christ. But man is simple and superstitious, and puts the power in the picture. The brazen serpent, a picture of Christ, became an idol, Nehushtan ([[2 Kings 18:4]]).
p: The dietary laws were a living parable, *to make a difference between the unclean and the clean* ([[Leviticus 11:47]]). Done away in Christ: *What God hath cleansed, that call not thou common* ([[Acts 10:15]]).

# from 5181, 15951
--- The sabbath fulfilled in Christ
kicker: Ordinances a shadow
big: Hebrews 4:9-10 | mark: For he that is entered into his rest, he also hath ceased from his own works
p: A picture of not working on the day of rest: we are entered into the Sabbath of Christ without works, but faith alone. Our works aren't needed, except to do good, to do the will of the Father.
p: The Lord of the Sabbath calls us to take the time, ceasing from our labors to help others. Not to be a burden, but to lift others from theirs. To rest in Jesus. *Call the sabbath a delight* ([[Isaiah 58:13]]).

# from 3095, 3070
--- Circumcision is nothing
kicker: Ordinances a shadow
big: Galatians 5:6 | mark: neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision; but faith which worketh by love
p: It's not the act of circumcision but the heart of those seeking justification with God through it, being placed in bondage under the yoke of the law. So Titus was not to be circumcised ([[Galatians 2:3-5]]).
p: But Paul circumcised Timothy, half-Gentile, raised Jewish, that he would not be hindered by the Jews when giving the Gospel ([[Acts 16:3]]). In that case circumcision is nothing, because it's not being put forth as a condition of justification.
read: app:doctrine-law~9190 | Ordinances were pictures, not idols
read: app:doctrine-law~5181 | The sabbath fulfilled in Christ

=== The better covenant
# from 15870, 13270, 10205
--- The fault was with them
kicker: The better covenant
big: Hebrews 8:7-8 | mark: For finding fault with them
p: The old covenant was ended, not because the law given Moses was flawed. The flaw was in them. Moses was taught a song to teach the children of Israel that God knew they would break the covenant ([[Deuteronomy 31:19-21]]).
p: The ten commandments covenant has ended with Christ. The moral components remain, covered by the two great commandments. The law of death replaced with the law of liberty.

# from 9176, 8757, 8634, 8672
--- A better testament
kicker: The better covenant
big: Hebrews 8:6 | mark: the mediator of a better covenant, which was established upon better promises
p: Jesus wasn't there to patch their old garment, or to refill their old, dried and cracked bottles, but to give new wine in bottles fit to hold it ([[Luke 5:36-39]]). It doesn't say “except for the Jews.” Hebrews is literally written to them.
p: No longer a priesthood, we are all priests. No longer a temple, we are each a temple. No longer a human mediator, Jesus is our High Priest. No longer a vail between God and man, Jesus tore it forever. Not Sinai, but mount Sion ([[Hebrews 12:22]]).

# from 7133, 6916, 7132, 12331
--- The bondwoman and the free
kicker: The better covenant
big: Galatians 4:21-22 | mark: Tell me, ye that desire to be under the law, do ye not hear the law?
p: The Galatians were being swayed into another gospel, of bondage to the law. Being dragged back to Hagar, the bondwoman, and rejecting Sarah and the son of the promise. *Cast out the bondwoman and her son* ([[Galatians 4:30]]).
p: If you're sewing your own fig leaves, if you're offering the fruit of your garden instead of the firstling of the flock, repent. Hear the law. The law is made null by the death of Christ, just as a marriage by the death of the husband ([[Romans 7:4]]).

# from 6916 (kept in full at the author's word)
--- All works-based religion cast out
kicker: The better covenant
big: Genesis 21:10 | mark: Cast out this bondwoman and her son
p: Those under the law, using their own works to justify themselves before God, are cast out. Children of the bondwoman. This extends not only to those Jews who developed the Talmudic Judaism that spun out of the Pharisaical line after the resurrection of Jesus, but to all works-based false religion.
p: From the fig leaves in the garden to Cain bringing his vegetables and fruit that he labored to grow. Right unto today with Catholic sacrament and works, Buddhist and Hindu and Muslims. And of course Jews of every stripe. Ishmael is said to be the father of what would be Islam, accepting Jesus as a prophet but denying His sacrifice, to trust in their own works.
read: app:doctrine-law~6916 | Cast out the bondwoman and her son

# from 17377, 6615, 16444, 16445
--- Better promises
kicker: The better covenant
big: Hebrews 9:15 | mark: he is the mediator of the new testament
p: Spiritual salvation was always by grace through faith for individuals, while the national promises were always contingent on works. Missed opportunities didn't make God a liar when He promised them. He rightly withdrew them when those the promises were made to didn't keep up their end.
p: From Noah on, blessings, commandments and promises ([[Genesis 9:1-17]]). By the blood of Christ a new and better testament, built on better promises, that we have been reconciled despite our own transgression of the law.
read: app:doctrine-law~15870 | The flaw was with them
read: app:doctrine-law~9176 | New wine in new bottles: a better covenant
read: app:doctrine-law~7133 | Do ye not hear the law? The bondwoman and the free

=== Delight in His law
--- Delight in the Law of the LORD [title]
overline: The law & the covenants
heading: Delight in the Law
big: Romans 7:12 | mark: the law is holy, and the commandment holy, and just, and good
center: It is perfectly fair. It is holy. It is righteous. It stands today. And where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty.
